# Design tokens

When editing Astro components or CSS under `src/`:

1. Use variables from `src/styles/tokens.css` for colour, type, space, and
   radius (`--color-*`, `--font-*`, `--space-*`, `--radius`, widths).
2. Keep the type stack: Barlow Condensed (display), Barlow (body),
   IBM Plex Mono (mono).
3. Preserve the dark ground + gold accent look already defined by the tokens.
4. Do not introduce a new palette, Inter/Roboto/system-default font stacks,
   or large radius / heavy card chrome that fights the existing UI.
5. Prefer extending token usage over hard-coded one-off colours when a token
   already exists.
